  "summary": "Denes, Jindal, Mikhailiuk, and Mantiuk develop and validate a perceptual model for choosing resolution and refresh rate in adaptive rendering. The source combines psychophysical comparisons, eye-tracking measurements, judder-isolation experiments, model fitting, and real-time validation to show that motion velocity and predictability should guide refresh-rate/resolution trade-offs under limited rendering budgets.",
